---
// Egypt — Section 05: "The Book of the Dead"
// Intimate, dark section about the Egyptian afterlife journey.
// Text appears as if being deciphered (blur/opacity via GSAP).
---

<section
  id="afterlife"
  class="relative overflow-hidden bg-[var(--egypt-obsidian)] py-section"
  aria-labelledby="book-heading"
>
  <!-- Papyrus texture overlay -->
  <div
    class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 opacity-[0.03]"
    style='background-image: url(&apos;data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg width="60" height="60" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"%3E%3Cfilter id="n"%3E%3CfeTurbulence type="fractalNoise" baseFrequency="0.65" numOctaves="3" stitchTiles="stitch"/%3E%3C/filter%3E%3Crect width="100%25" height="100%25" filter="url(%23n)" opacity="1"/%3E%3C/svg%3E&apos;);'
    aria-hidden="true"
  >
  </div>

  <div
    class="relative mx-auto w-full max-w-landing px-container-x sm:px-8 xl:px-14"
  >
    <!-- Chapter marker -->
    <p
      class="mb-4 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--egypt-gold)]/60"
    >
      05 &mdash; The Book of the Dead
    </p>

    <h2
      id="book-heading"
      class="max-w-heading font-display text-headline-1 uppercase leading-none tracking-wider text-white"
    >
      Death Was Not the End
    </h2>

    <div class="mt-16 max-w-copy lg:mt-24">
      <p
        class="text-xl leading-relaxed text-[var(--egypt-sand)]/80 italic"
        data-decipher
      >
        It was a journey. A passage through darkness, through judgment, through
        transformation. The dead did not simply rest. They traveled.
      </p>

      <p
        class="mt-10 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--egypt-sand)]/60"
        data-decipher
      >
        The Book of the Dead was not a single text but a collection of spells,
        prayers, and instructions — a guide for navigating the underworld. Each
        copy was personalized, written on papyrus scrolls and placed inside the
        coffin with the deceased.
      </p>

      <p
        class="mt-8 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--egypt-sand)]/60"
        data-decipher
      >
        The spells guided the soul past demons, through gates guarded by
        serpents, across lakes of fire, and finally to the Hall of Ma'at — where
        the ultimate judgment awaited.
      </p>

      <blockquote
        class="mt-12 border-l-2 border-[var(--egypt-gold)]/30 pl-6"
        data-decipher
      >
        <p
          class="font-display text-headline-3 uppercase leading-snug tracking-wide text-[var(--egypt-gold)]"
        >
          "I have not done iniquity. I have not robbed with violence. I have not
          done violence to any man. I have not committed theft."
        </p>
        <cite class="mt-4 block text-sm text-[var(--egypt-sand)]/50 not-italic">
          — The Negative Confession, Spell 125, Book of the Dead
        </cite>
      </blockquote>

      <p
        class="mt-10 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--egypt-sand)]/60"
        data-decipher
      >
        To pass, the deceased had to recite the Negative Confession — a
        declaration of innocence before forty-two divine judges. Each denial was
        specific. Each was a moral inventory of an entire life.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
